/-!
# Flatness is stable under completed base change (Stacks 0GCA)

Let `B → A` be a flat morphism and `B → C` a morphism, both between Noetherian adic topological
rings. **Stacks 0GCA** says that the completed tensor product `A ⊗̂_B C` is again Noetherian adic
and flat over `C`, in two situations:

1. `B → C` is of finite type on reductions (Stacks 0GC2): the local property of Stacks 0GC9 is
   stable under base change by the local property of Stacks 0GC2, in the sense of Remark 0GBG;
2. `B → A` is moreover adic and topologically of finite type (Stacks 0GBW), and `B → C` is
   arbitrary: flatness together with the property of Stacks 0GBW is stable under base change in
   the sense of Remark 0GBF, so `C → A ⊗̂_B C` is again flat, adic and topologically of finite
   type.

Flatness over `C` is proved in both parts by exhibiting `A ⊗̂_B C` as the limit of the tower of
adic completions

```
T_n = (A ⊗_B C/J^n)^∧   (completion for the ideal generated by an ideal of definition of A)
```

for an ideal of definition `J ⊆ C`.  Each `T_n` is flat over `C/J^n`: `A ⊗_B C/J^n` is flat over
`C/J^n` because `A` is flat over `B`, and its adic completion is flat over it because it is
Noetherian.  The transition maps `T_{n+1} → T_n` are surjective, so Tag 0912 applies and the
limit is flat over `C`.  The two parts differ in why `A ⊗_B C/J^n` is Noetherian: in part (1)
`C/J^n` is of finite type over `B` by Tag 0GC6, so `A ⊗_B C/J^n` is of finite type over `A`; in
part (2) some power `I^k` of an ideal of definition of `B` dies in `C/J^n` while `I^k A` is open
in `A`, so `A ⊗_B C/J^n` is a quotient of `C/J^n ⊗_B A/I^kA`, of finite type over `C/J^n`.

## Main results

* `TopologicalRing.completedTensorProduct_isNoetherianRing_of_isFiniteTypeOnReductions`: a
  completed tensor product of pre-adic Noetherian algebras is Noetherian as soon as *either*
  structure morphism is of finite type on reductions.
* `TopologicalRing.flat_isStableUnderBaseChangeByFiniteTypeOnReductions`: **Stacks 0GCA, part
  (1)**.
* `TopologicalRing.PropertyIsLocal.and`: the conjunction of two local properties is local.
* `TopologicalRing.flatAdicFiniteType_isStableUnderBaseChange`: **Stacks 0GCA, part (2)**.

## Implementation notes

The double inverse limit `lim_{m,n} (A/I^m) ⊗_B (C/J^n)` of
`TopologicalRing.quotientLimit` identifies `A ⊗̂_B C` with the limit of the tower `T_n`: fixing
`n` and letting `m` vary gives the adic completion `T_n`, and `tensorStageProjection` is that
comparison.  All the intermediate maps are built from ring homomorphisms rather than from the
`AdicCompletion.map` of a linear map, because the limit has to be taken in `ModuleCat C` while
the compatibility is a ring-level statement; `completionRingMap_eq_linearMap` identifies the two
constructions where surjectivity of a transition map has to be read off.

Tag 0GB4's Noetherianity statement is asymmetric — it asks for finite type of the quotient map
out of the *first* factor.  The symmetric form is obtained from it by transporting along
`TopologicalRing.completedTensorProductComm`.  Part (2) uses it for the first factor, through
Tag 0GC5: an adic morphism topologically of finite type is of finite type on reductions.

In part (2) the stages `A ⊗_B C/J^n` are already `I`-adically discrete, so `T_n` is
`A ⊗_B C/J^n` itself, as the source remarks; the proof does not need this and runs the same
tower argument as part (1).

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0GCA](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0GCA)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0GB4](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0GB4)
